course: dictionary
lesson: 8529
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. The context tells you which meaning the author means. «Checking before you challenge saves you from being wrong in front of everyone.» Here saves means keeps you from something bad, not that you are putting money by.
explain: Sport words give the clue in a different sentence. «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» Goal and penalty tell you that saved means he stopped the ball from going in.
explain: Some clues come from the idea of the whole sentence. «A hedgehog... may breathe only a few times a minute; it is not just sleeping, its whole body has slowed down to save energy.» Save here means use less of something, because the body slows down. When you find a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence and choose the one that fits best.
fact: «Save» is a verb and a noun: you can save money, or you can make a save in sport.
fact: To save money is to keep it instead of spending it, so you have more later. «Saving means putting money aside, week after week.»
fact: To save someone is to keep them safe from danger, as in «save a life».
fact: To save time, water or energy is to use less of it.
fact: On a computer, to save a file means to store it. In football or hockey, a save is when the goalkeeper stops the ball.
exercise: In «Then he went in goal... and saved a penalty», what does saved mean? | Stored it on a computer | Kept the money for later | *Stopped the ball from going in | Used less of it
exercise: The hedgehog's whole body has slowed down to save energy. What does save mean here? | Stop the ball | Store a file | Keep money for later | *Use less of it
exercise: Mum says, «Let's save up for a new bike.» What does save up mean? | *Put money aside, bit by bit, for later | Stop the ball in goal | Keep someone safe from danger | Spend all the money now
test: «Checking before you challenge saves you from being wrong in front of everyone.» What does saves mean here? | *Keeps you away from something bad | Puts money by for later | Stores the file | Stops a ball
test: Ella says, «Save your work before you shut the laptop.» What does save mean? | Stop the ball | Spend it | Use less of it | *Store it on the computer so it is kept
exam: «Messages can be saved, shared and misunderstood, so you never send what you would not say face to face.» What does saved mean in this sentence? | Spent | Shared | Used up | *Stored, so they can be kept and found later
